' steps
' User is logged in (JWT authentication).
' User adds products to the shopping cart.
' User chooses to place an order.
' System checks whether the user is authenticated.
' CreateOrder() is called.
' OrderService.CreateOrderAsync() calls OrderRepository.CreateOrder().
' A database transaction starts.
' A new order is created with status Pending.
' Cart items are copied to order_items.
' Shopping cart items are removed.
' An entry is added to order_status_history.
' Transaction commits.
' User receives success response.
' User can optionally create a payment afterwards.
' User can later view, cancel, or track the order.


@startuml

start

:User is authenticated;

:View shopping cart;

:Add products to cart;

:Submit order;

:Start database transaction;

:Create order
(Status = Pending);

if (Order created?) then (Yes)

    :Copy cart items
    to order_items;

    if (Items copied?) then (Yes)

        :Delete cart items;

        :Insert order status history;

        :Commit transaction;

        :Return success;

        :Optional:
        Create payment;

    else (No)

        :Rollback transaction;
        :Return error;

    endif

else (No)

    :Rollback transaction;
    :Return error;

endif

stop

@enduml